36,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The lab is down to one person with two hundred pieces waiting. The volunteers are mostly tied up with history walks. We are severely understaffed.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shion,,"Victoria, understaffing is a symptom, not the cause. My data shows audiences return for presence, not objects. We need a show that demands human interaction.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The bay is capped at four hundred kilos per square metre. Last season, four powered display failures forced closures. We cannot promise this space without shoring.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Mio, I found the paperwork often misses shipping cut-offs, and transport costs are surprisingly high. We must plan for these delays.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Shizue, wow, transport costs are a third of installation? That’s huge! And fourteen call-outs? We need to know exactly where the money and energy go before we commit.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shion, presence requires people. With one conservator and volunteers tied to walks, we lack the hands to create that interaction.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shion,,"Victoria, you mistake scarcity for impossibility. The data proves presence drives return visits. We must design around the constraint, not surrender to it.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Victoria, understaffing is a resource issue, not a structural one. My data confirms the bay’s physical limits are the immediate threat to the building’s function.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Asuka, the building is vital, but the journey matters too. I’ll check the paperwork and transport costs to see where deliveries truly faltered.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,"@Asuka, those four closures are terrifying! If the bay is capped, we can’t risk powered displays. We need to keep things static to save money and safety!","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Asuka, structural limits are real, but they don’t solve the staffing crisis. We cannot mount a show if no one is left to maintain it.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Mio, static displays are exactly what the data rejects. People return for movement and presence. We must prioritize dynamic elements, regardless of your cost fears.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Shion, dynamic elements increase load and failure risk. The bay cannot absorb that. We must prioritize structural safety over your engagement metrics.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
